  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "kO0G09HIQmCH0vk1IKKLln+uwAM=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:30:39.736Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "XTi has delivered Java and open-source custom development since 2001, which the record summarises as OSS-native, and it is dual-certified: Camunda Silver and Flowable Strategic. It operates from three Belgian locations \u2014 Kontich, Hasselt and Merelbeke \u2014 and is carried at priority 2.\n\nThe reason the track record matters more than the certifications is that open-source posture is the criterion the screen most often cannot evidence. Elsewhere in the same sweep the instruction is to run an OSS-portfolio screen before acting, precisely because a platform certification says nothing about whether a firm would build on client-owned, open infrastructure. A quarter-century of open-source custom delivery answers that question from history rather than from a positioning statement, which is stronger evidence than any partner tier.\n\nThe dual certification then adds the practical seam: both Camunda and Flowable are orchestration engines that decide when things happen while holding the running instance as mutable, purgeable state, so both leave the append-only decision record unowned. A firm certified on both has the same gap twice, and the integration built for one applies to the other. Provenance is the Flowable Partner Finder mined on 2026-08-18, not imprint-swept.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**2 \u00b7 next**\n- XTi NV (BE Kontich/Hasselt/Merelbeke) \u2014 xt-i.com\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> Java + open source custom dev since 2001 \u2014 OSS-native. DUAL: Camunda Silver + Flowable Strategic \u00b7 SOURCE: Flowable Partner Finder (flowable.com/company/partners), mined 2026-08-18. NOT imprint-swept.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:30:39.736680Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:30:39.736684Z"
    }
  },
